{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/compare/master...e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","html_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/compare/master...e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","permalink_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/compare/jqlang:5c001b1...jqlang:e47e56d","diff_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/compare/master...e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/compare/master...e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"5c001b18d7237cce1fdba63608732163f978dd23","node_id":"C_kwDOAE3WVdoAKDVjMDAxYjE4ZDcyMzdjY2UxZmRiYTYzNjA4NzMyMTYzZjk3OGRkMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"itchyny","email":"itchyny@cybozu.co.jp","date":"2026-11-02T07:08:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-02T07:08:10Z"},"message":"Fix mktime/0 to allow the last two seconds of 1969 (#3671)\n\nThe mktime/0 function failed for 1969-12-31T23:59:59Z with \"invalid\ngmtime representation\", because its result -1 is also the failure value\nof timegm(), and for 1969-12-31T23:59:58Z with \"mktime not supported on\nthis platform\", because of a leftover check for -2.\n\nTell a failure apart from the valid result -1 by tm_wday, which is set\nto -1 before the conversion and overwritten only on success, and remove\nthe check for -2. Now `-2, -1 | gmtime | mktime` round-trip to -2 and -1,\nas do normalized inputs such as [1970,0,0,23,59,59,0,0], which gives -1.\nInputs that the platform rejects, such as years before 1900 on macOS,\nstill fail with \"invalid gmtime representation\".","tree":{"sha":"5725751efef562a5287d0f42c2a1ef6cf0a5f21b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/git/trees/5725751efef562a5287d0f42c2a1ef6cf0a5f21b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/git/commits/5c001b18d7237cce1fdba63608732163f978dd23","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq6DbaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1ZMQAKAfLqffEXkErRjiu88Rfu4/\nxR9diO8W3wDO/GDqsf0EiaaVQujkHZF261KmSQ/lIMW5ZacMva1acOKTewMa0jwL\nqmXjs30tr+FJnm5gesUnkIC37kKrWNnDHeouolDh7MwZOhoUxVnhaA1kKGHd9cpi\nzmaGYN8SDfx+fd3so1/E6F3xWrAO/k22iauoxT3wv5On1pgmcUfH60SZQi+2R6UJ\ny/MKjjFKgq8tajLMbeIuFoNuBuCEPqVPPQqFNg/Kfp654pCYVKydcP4FesNkE1KG\nCNItvop82NSwNoc2n3l7JH1GDz99k1c7Ct9Lzsygca2tB0cVPh4W+jINN9GQP1x+\nKhcMnJZwIy7IU6hbHxvZKjZN3vyxXpt81cLqbCnp4484SXh5FADEQGqoaoePGlCy\n4OB8ZwRsKMW+B9EQ9/KDs8hC1tYmsfJLm7GuGnUSdui2jJoliUoVZ4Xt/QLr8SRT\n8UkQXNtNWOvACVeLDyH28LveLkEIp18IcFRuG5T1HmFciLK/613kDZfloTVDrojZ\nOFRwFtZDbvy/IB2tWOzCtL0VK7ArxhzCNo+xbA/TjvAx/j7KuEAKV+jv/4mlrMbN\nUz6SMv7Y0eW27oh0pX4AI4tItiZEt6zdFfDFMztazjHqRcccXRINlR3gV3KM/K7b\njq1BpowfymBWvNm2i5US\n=HM7j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5725751efef562a5287d0f42c2a1ef6cf0a5f21b\nparent 992db9b7e5e3059b764bf430bd97716829e99578\nauthor itchyny <itchyny@cybozu.co.jp> 1793603290 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793603290 +0900\n\nFix mktime/0 to allow the last two seconds of 1969 (#3671)\n\nThe mktime/0 function failed for 1969-12-31T23:59:59Z with \"invalid\ngmtime representation\", because its result -1 is also the failure value\nof timegm(), and for 1969-12-31T23:59:58Z with \"mktime not supported on\nthis platform\", because of a leftover check for -2.\n\nTell a failure apart from the valid result -1 by tm_wday, which is set\nto -1 before the conversion and overwritten only on success, and remove\nthe check for -2. Now `-2, -1 | gmtime | mktime` round-trip to -2 and -1,\nas do normalized inputs such as [1970,0,0,23,59,59,0,0], which gives -1.\nInputs that the platform rejects, such as years before 1900 on macOS,\nstill fail with \"invalid gmtime representation\".","verified_at":"2026-11-02T07:08:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/commits/5c001b18d7237cce1fdba63608732163f978dd23","html_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/commit/5c001b18d7237cce1fdba63608732163f978dd23","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/commits/5c001b18d7237cce1fdba63608732163f978dd23/comments","author":{"login":"itchyny","id":375258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTI1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/375258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny","html_url":"https://github.com/itchyny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itchyny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"992db9b7e5e3059b764bf430bd97716829e99578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/commits/992db9b7e5e3059b764bf430bd97716829e99578","html_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/commit/992db9b7e5e3059b764bf430bd97716829e99578"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","node_id":"C_kwDOAE3WVdoAKGU0N2U1NmQyMjY1MTk2MzU3NjhlNmFhYjJmMzhmMGFiMDM3YzA5ZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"itchyny","email":"itchyny@cybozu.co.jp","date":"2026-03-12T11:28:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"itchyny","email":"itchyny@cybozu.co.jp","date":"2026-04-12T23:27:16Z"},"message":"Fix heap buffer overflow in `jvp_string_append` and `jvp_string_copy_replace_bad`\n\nIn `jvp_string_append`, the allocation size `(currlen + len) * 2` could\noverflow `uint32_t` when `currlen + len` exceeds `INT_MAX`, causing a small\nallocation followed by a large `memcpy`.\n\nIn `jvp_string_copy_replace_bad`, the output buffer size calculation\n`length * 3 + 1` could overflow `uint32_t`, again resulting in a small\nallocation followed by a large write.\n\nAdd overflow checks to both functions to return an error for strings\nthat would exceed `INT_MAX` in length. Fixes CVE-2026-32316.","tree":{"sha":"5652b3967fed6232f742b11515ebb5a33f453f05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/git/trees/5652b3967fed6232f742b11515ebb5a33f453f05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/git/commits/e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/commits/e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","html_url":"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/commit/e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq/commits/e47e56d226519635768e6aab2f38f0ab037c09e5/comments","author":{"login":"itchyny","id":375258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTI1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/375258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.git